  ('15eb0cf4-6c62-40de-993b-95d549b915c5', '67d56190-5f8b-4b38-bd62-cc422ad87887', 'TG_MOV_MOCK2_040', 'The slogan "Idli-Sambar Go Back" specifically targeted officials and staff arriving from which region?', 'Bombay State', 'Madras State (including Coastal Andhra)', 'Mysore State', 'Central Provinces', 'At that time (1952), Coastal Andhra was part of the composite Madras State (prior to the formation of Andhra State in Oct 1953). Immigrant officers from the Madras Presidency brought their culinary culture, prompting this popular student slogan.', '40 [Direct Factual / ప్రత్యక్ష ప్రశ్న]
